+## Requirements
+Use the labels G1 to G5 in your report.
+
+1. **G1. Every escape decoded.** For both `gh api` refusals G2 and G3 read, each word is first decoded: every `%` followed by two hexadecimal digits (either case) is replaced by the character those digits name, and the decoding is repeated on its result until a pass changes nothing (a doubly escaped `%2570` reads as `p`: an over-refusal at worst, never a miss). Decode with `re.sub` over `%([0-9A-Fa-f]{2})` (no new import). A word that is not ASCII after decoding is read as it is.
+2. **G2. The merge endpoint read from the path, as written and resolved.** Lower-case the decoded word. Cut it at its first `?` or `#` (the part before is the path; the whole word if it holds neither). Refuse the command, with round 1's text (`gh api on a pull request's merge endpoint (merging outside the gate)`), where any of these three holds `/pulls/<segment>/merge` (`<segment>` one or more characters other than `/`): the decoded lower-cased word whole; its path; its path through `posixpath.normpath`. Reading the whole word as well keeps every word f3fa7b4 refused refused.
+3. **G3. The merge mutations read in the decoded words.** The merge-mutation refusal looks for each name of `MERGE_MUTATIONS` in each word as written **and** in its decoded form (G1, case kept: GraphQL names are case-sensitive), with its text unchanged.
